00:09:11.071 --> 00:09:13.490
We brine the chicken in a
buttermilk solution for a day,

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:15.559
the buttermilk helps
tenderize it, gives it flavor.

00:09:15.559 --> 00:09:18.346
Great fried chicken is about
getting fissures as it fries.

00:09:18.346 --> 00:09:21.282
Doing this is about creating
irregularity in the batter.

00:09:21.282 --> 00:09:23.954
We've created a dredge
for it of flour, spices.

00:09:23.954 --> 00:09:25.162
And then when fry it whole.

00:09:25.162 --> 00:09:26.854
We let it rest for at least 30 minutes,

00:09:26.854 --> 00:09:28.138
because you don't want it super hot.

00:09:28.138 --> 00:09:30.042
Create all the sauces and the garnish.

00:09:30.042 --> 00:09:32.646
Scallion crepes, white sauce,
chives, and creme fraise.

00:09:32.646 --> 00:09:33.896
We're preparing it with what I believe is

00:09:33.896 --> 00:09:36.514
the best domestic caviar, by Regalis.

00:09:36.514 --> 00:09:37.483
Some of the most beautiful Sturgeon.

00:09:37.483 --> 00:09:39.627
We're also gonna pair it
with some smoked Trout roe.

00:09:39.627 --> 00:09:41.602
The salinity and oceanic brininess

00:09:41.602 --> 00:09:44.034
of the caviar is perfect
for the white meat.

00:09:44.034 --> 00:09:45.746
Present it table side, show it to you,

00:09:45.746 --> 00:09:47.475
